sequenceDiagram
    title BLE Central Bonded Reconnection: Re-encrypt with Stored Keys

    participant App as App
    participant Node as Node<br>[implements GapCentral]
    participant Peripheral as BLE Peripheral


    Note over Node, Peripheral: Messages between Node and BLE Peripheral are link-layer events, not driven by the App.<br>The App only observes them through Echo callbacks (e.g. CurrentState).

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Peripheral: 1. Locate the bonded peripheral (optional)
        opt App does not already know the target and scans first
            App->>Node: GapCentral.StartDeviceDiscovery()
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(scanning)
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.DeviceDiscovered(<br>addressWithType={address=6C:8B:2F:3A:9D:41, addressType=randomAddress},<br>rssi=-42)
            App->>Node: GapCentral.Standby()
            Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(standby)
        end

        Note over App: Alternatively, Connect(bond.identityAddress) directly.<br>The controller matches incoming/observed RPAs via the LL resolving list<br>(populated with the peer's IRK at bond time).
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Peripheral: 2. Reconnect
        App->>Node: GapCentral.Connect(<br>addressWithType={address=6C:8B:2F:3A:9D:41, addressType=randomAddress},<br>initiatingTimeoutInMs=5000)
        Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(initiating)
        Node-)Peripheral: CONNECT_IND (unacknowledged)
        Note over Node, Peripheral: Central assumes the connection has started once CONNECT_IND is sent.<br>The link is confirmed only by the first bidirectional data exchange in a connection event.<br>For a bonded peer, the LL resolves the RPA via the stored IRK before sending CONNECT_IND.
        Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.CurrentState(connected)
        Note over App, Node: The exact moment CurrentState(connected) fires is stack-dependent —<br>some stacks emit it on CONNECT_IND transmit, others wait for the first successful data exchange.
    end

    rect rgb(230, 230, 240)
        note over App, Peripheral: 3. Re-encryption
        App->>Node: GapCentral.PairAndBond()
        rect rgb(245, 240, 230)
            Note over Node, Peripheral: LL encryption using the stored LTK (no SMP)
            Node-)Peripheral: LL_ENC_REQ (Rand, EDIV, SKD_M, IV_M)
            Peripheral-)Node: LL_ENC_RSP (SKD_S, IV_S)
            Peripheral-)Node: LL_START_ENC_REQ (encrypted)
            Node-)Peripheral: LL_START_ENC_RSP (encrypted)
            Peripheral-)Node: LL_START_ENC_RSP (encrypted)
        end
        Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.NumberOfBondsChanged(1)
        Node-->>App: GapCentralResponse.PairingResult(pairedSuccessfully=true)

        Note over App: PairAndBond is required. Without it the link stays unencrypted.<br>Existing bond is reused, so no SMP user interaction (no AuthenticationRequired).<br>NumberOfBondsChanged signals the LRU aging update — the bond count is unchanged.
    end
